# An explicit npmignore, even though package.json has a `files` allowlist.
#
# `files` is what actually decides the tarball. This file exists so that npm never
# falls back to .gitignore — which it did, silently, and which shipped
# .claude/settings.local.json (326 permission entries naming absolute home paths and
# localhost ports) while EXCLUDING contracts/managed/ that the runtime needs. Belt and
# braces on a mistake that is invisible until someone downloads the package.
#
# Anything not listed in `files` is excluded regardless. These are the entries worth
# naming so the intent is readable.

.claude/
notes/
web/
scripts/
src/
patches/
docker-compose*.yml
tsconfig*.json
.midnight-*
midnight-level-db/
*.tsbuildinfo
